{"game": "arc-raiders", "language": "english", "appid": 1808500, "month": "2026-05", "window": 4, "start_date": 1779580800, "end_date": 1780271999, "month_true_total": 6257, "quota": 9, "returned": 9, "pulled_at": "2026-09-10 21:19:03 Pacific Daylight Time", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "226907648", "author": {"steamid": "76561198299350658", "personaname": "RustiSqueezebox", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/RustiSqueezebox/", "num_games_owned": 754, "num_reviews": 13, "playtime_forever": 33958, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 504, "playtime_at_review": 24799, "last_played": 1789100075, "avatar": "0f0bf48c85137887655637d1d28e071c6c65d4bc"}, "language": "english", "review": "I’ve really been enjoying Arc Raiders. The combat is one of the strongest parts of the game because it rewards both skill and tactical decision-making. Every encounter feels engaging, whether it’s choosing when to push a fight, reposition, or work around other players and environmental threats. When everything clicks, the combat feels incredibly satisfying.\r\n\r\nOne of my favorite parts of the experience has been running into other kind raiders. Those unexpected positive interactions add a unique layer to the game and create memorable moments that make each run feel different.\r\n\r\nThe looting system is also a lot of fun. There’s something really satisfying about scavenging, making quick decisions about what’s worth taking, and trying to extract successfully while balancing risk versus reward.\r\n\r\nMy main criticism right now is that it sometimes feels like there isn’t enough to work toward long term. The quest system can feel unrewarding at times, and I’d love to see stronger progression incentives or more meaningful objectives to keep that long-term motivation going.\r\n\r\nOverall though, Arc Raiders has a really solid foundation. The gameplay loop is enjoyable, the combat feels great, and with more rewarding progression, I think it has the potential to be something special.", "timestamp_created": 1780271498, "timestamp_updated": 1780271498, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1761816609", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "226907280", "author": {"steamid": "76561198155504357", "personaname": "Usuário da Perdição", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198155504357/", "num_games_owned": 95, "num_reviews": 6, "playtime_forever": 23890, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 15359, "last_played": 1787884498, "avatar": "3e7fa82d331c950cc2dffca68c4e0f723849cff0"}, "language": "english", "review": "The main hub should be called despair instead of Speranza. \r\nNo PVE ? Bad review\r\nGreat concept, amazing ai and enviroment, full of rats. Just make an exclusive PVE mode and all the players who left will come back. Notice that the people who defend Pvp just want to kill peaceful PvE players like me and dont want to fight other PvP players like them. So brave, these rats.\r\nIll tell you what will happen in the next 6 months as you idiots in Embark are too blind to see it somehow.\r\nThe game is so full of cheaters eventually even the honest PvP players will leave, then all the rats and cheaters will flood the PvE lobbies and your fake-ass retarded karma system will collapse making the last PvE players leave the game. Then the game will only be played by rats and cheaters agains rats and cheaters, making all the PvE content, quests and achievements undoable as everyone will be locked in the rat infested hell, which will in turn leave to a bad review bombing and mass exodus, killing the game definitely.\r\nGreat game, ♥♥♥♥ developer. You gonna die and that is what you deserve", "timestamp_created": 1780271062, "timestamp_updated": 17